---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Install the Hearth skill for development"
  description="Link the Hearth skill with the repository install script."
  locale="en"
  path="/install/skill"
>
  <p class="text-ink/70 text-sm font-medium tracking-wider uppercase">Setup · Skill</p>
  <h1>Add the Hearth skill<br/>to Claude Code.</h1>
  <p>This is a developer installation path that uses the Hearth repository source.</p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/withgenie/hearth.git
cd hearth
./scripts/install-skills.sh --into ~/.claude/skills</code></pre>

  <h2>What happens</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>~/.claude/skills/hearth/</code> is created.</li>
    <li>The repository skill and supporting files are linked there.</li>
    <li>The next Claude Code session picks it up automatically.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <p>Call it in natural language. e.g. <em>"Leave a memo in Hearth — agenda for tomorrow's meeting."</em></p>

  <h2>Uninstall</h2>
  <pre><code>./scripts/install-skills.sh --into ~/.claude/skills --remove</code></pre>
</Base>
